.TH EDIT 1
.SH NAME
edit \- simple text editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B wm/edit
.RI [ file ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Edit
is a simple cut-and-paste text editor in a
.IR wm (1)
window.
It is the editor Inferno has always shipped as
.BR wm/edit ;
programs that load
.B /dis/wm/edit.dis
to show a file
(for instance the
.B Files
button of
.BR wm/task ,
which shows a process's open files)
get it.
.IR Editor (1),
with its 9P interface for agents, is a different program.
.PP
If a
.I file
is named, it is opened; a name that does not exist yet is taken as a new
file of that name, written by
.BR Save .
.PP
The
.B File
menu has
.BR New ,
.BR Open...
(a file browser in columns),
.BR Save ,
.B "Save As..."
and
.BR Exit .
The
.B Edit
menu has
.BR Cut ,
.B Copy
and
.BR Paste ,
through the
.IR wm (1)
snarf buffer.
The
.B Search
menu finds a string, sets a replacement, finds again, and replaces
one match or all of them.
Under
.BR Options ,
.B Limbo
colours keywords and comments and indents blocks as they are typed;
.B Indent
sets the text of one level of indentation.
.PP
Text is selected by dragging with mouse button 1.
Button 2 pops up the
.B Edit
menu.
The arrow, page and home keys move the insertion point without marking the
file changed.
Leaving, opening or starting another file when the text has changed asks
first.
The window takes the current Lucifer theme, and follows a switch of it.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/wm/edit.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR editor (1),
.IR acme (1),
.IR wm (1)
